 459| #### 2.4.1 The genome screens and clearance
 464| A rotor tip below 1.5 m of ground clearance fails the clearance gate (NR-042).
 467| #### 2.4.2 The rope break
 470| A strain past the break strain ends the run and rejects the design (NR-013).
 472| Detection off the window would reject healthy machines, and section 4.1 holds that record.
 474| #### 2.4.3 The twist crossing
 476| The twist gate reads the worst segment twist against the geometric crossing limit (NR-052, NR-053).
 480| #### 2.4.4 The tip-speed ceiling
 482| Every ring rim and every rotor tip carries a speed ceiling of 100.0 m/s (NR-047).
 485| #### 2.4.5 The three Betz screens
 488| The per-rotor screen compares each rotor against the Betz limit on its own bank-projected annulus (NR-034).
 489| The availability screen compares power against a coefficient floor on the normal wind area, below the power floor (NR-027, NR-034).
 490| The aggregate screen compares the window-mean power against the Betz limit on the total area (NR-034).
 500| The screen is a loose tripwire (NR-034).
 502| The availability and aggregate screens read the wind-normal area, which carries the elevation factor (NR-034).
 505| Section 3.3 carries the ceiling value.
 508| #### 2.4.6 The power floor and the safety floor
 510| The power floor reads the window-end power against 5.0 kW (NR-027, NR-039).
 511| The safety floor reads the window-minimum factor of safety against 2.5 (NR-015).
 515| A torsional safety floor of 1.5 belongs to the design-verification path (NR-052).
 516| The two campaign floors read 5.0 kW and 2.5.
 518| #### 2.4.7 The objective and its four charges
 523| One kilogram of airborne mass adds 1.0 to the score (NR-046).
 528| The score adds three charges to the airborne mass (NR-046):
 530| $$f=\mathrm{mass}+5.0\max\left(P_{\mathrm{score}}-5.0,\,0\right)^{2}+20.0\left(\frac{2.5}{\mathrm{FoS}_{\min}}\right)^{2}+1.0\left(\frac{r}{1-r}\right)^{2}$$
 532| The ratio reads $r=\min\left(\mathrm{twist\_ratio},\,1\right)$.
 533| The score then adds the stationarity charge (NR-046):
 535| $$10.0\max\left(0,\,\mathrm{swing}-0.20\right)$$
 540| The over-power charge reads P_score, the end power, against the 5.0 kW ceiling (NR-046).
 541| The utilisation charge reads the window-minimum factor of safety against the 2.5 floor (NR-046).
 542| The twist charge reads the worst segment twist ratio against the crossing limit (NR-046).
 543| The stationarity charge reads the window swing against 20 per cent (NR-046).
 544| The winner carries all four in its own score: mass plus 0.4933, 0.5577 and 0.6141, and a stationarity charge of zero (NR-039).
 546| The swing reads P_range over P_mean, the window power range over its mean (NR-046).
 549| ratio r over (1 minus r) would divide by zero.
