1152| ## 5 Conclusion
1154| The report screened 930 rigid-wing ground-generation rotary kite turbine designs with a tensile rotary power transmission (NR-001).
1155| The campaign scored each design on the ODE path over the measurement window (NR-015).
1156| One fixed power-law generator load and one fixed gate set held for every design (NR-015).
1158| The search found 508 feasible candidates in the searched space (NR-002).
1159| The 301 rejects split three ways (NR-055).
1160| 96 ran below the 5 kW power floor.
1161| Four ran at or above 5 kW with a factor of safety below 2.5.
1162| The remaining 201 carried no logged cause at campaign time.
1164| The re-run probe (NR-061) names them.
1165| 93 rotors cannot reach 80 per cent of the power floor on their swept area and power coefficient.
1166| 37 settle at the realisability cliff.
1168| 36 refuse on rotor spacing.
1169| 30 break a line at the rope-break gate, not a beam FoS breach or a twist crossing (NR-013).
1174| objective and the gates, reads 5.309 kW of mean mechanical power (NR-008).
1175| All checked TRPT rings and twist segments operate below their failure boundaries at the final operating point (NR-021, NR-022).
1181| The rapid path takes the rope-break gate placement fix (NR-013 ext2).
1185| The recommended next steps sit in section 3.6.
1201| The programme targets larger machines, 7 to 50 kW.
1206| axial-length study runs to 60 m as a plan probe. That figure is not a
